            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0256" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2091b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-09T14:00:00-05:00">October 9, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>372. 1. Repeat to Peck Department’s 367, October 7, 8 p.m.<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d154-f1"/></p>
                <p>2. Inform Peck that the Secretary of State had a long conversation with the
                    Chinese Chargé on October 8. The Secretary explained our attitude and policy and
                    urged necessity for self-control on part of both the Japanese and the Chinese
                    nations. He has repeatedly urged same on Japanese Ambassador.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
